{
  "case_id": "2021-20-843",
  "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Clement, how could it stop there? In Heller, we made very clear that laws that restricted felons from carrying or possessing arms and laws that forbade mentally ill people from doing the same -- we, you know, basically put the stamp of approval on those laws. And those laws really came about in the 1920s, didn't they?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Those surety laws, which were only in --in -- in place in a minority of jurisdictions, but, nonetheless, I think they help us because those surety laws, first of all, start with the proposition that there's a baseline right for every person, every member of the people, protected by the Second Amendment, to carry."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Well, what sort of place do you think they could be excluded from? In other words, you can get a permit, but the state can impose certain restrictions, for example, any place in which alcohol is served."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So here -- here's what I would suggest, that the right way to think about limiting guns in Times Square on New Year's Eve is not as a sensitive place but as a time, place, and manner restriction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: -- could we start with the purpose of the personal right to keep and bear arms? And the core purpose of that right, putting aside the military aspect, is self-defense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: Justice Alito, that might be a way of analyzing it. The reason I'm a little bit reluctant to go that route as opposed to really think about the nature of the place and the restrictions that are associated with its core activity is because I worry that, if you went that direction, then the state would say: Well, you know, this part of the city, we have a lot of police officers, and so you really don't need to exercise your own individual self-defense right there because we -- we have your back."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Clement, you -- you said, I think, in passing that it would be fine if New York banned open carry so long as it allowed concealed carry. Is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: Certainly, that's consistent with the relief we're looking for. We're looking for some outlet to exercise our constitutional right to carry firearms outside the home."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Some of your amici have asked us to provide further guidance to lower courts in cases beyond your own. And so, putting aside your -- your case for the moment, they've pointed out that some lower courts have refused to apply the history test, for example, and said they will not extend Heller outside the home until this Court does."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, I want to make sure I understand your main problem here with this permitting regime, as I understand it, is the discretion that's involved with the permitting officials, and your point that that's just not how we do constitutional rights, where we allow basic blanket discretion to grant or deny something for all sorts of reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. Underwood",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't know, but I will tell you that our licensing officer told us that rapes and -- and robberies happen on the deserted bike paths and that he has some concern about that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. Underwood",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "to self-defense doesn't -- as -- as this Court said, doesn't allow for all to -- to be armed for all possible confrontations in all places."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think that's an irrelevant word?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. Underwood",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0004-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "we have substantial authority for the proposition that guns were deemed to be offensive weapons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0004-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I don't want to belabor the point, but, of course, if any possession of weapons outside the home was illegal, then there would be no need to put in the term \"offensively,\" the inclusion of that term."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Brian H. Fletcher",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0004-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 92,
        "start": 92
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "New York's proper cause requirement is consistent with the Second Amendment because it is firmly grounded in our nation's history and tradition of gun regulation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Brian H. Fletcher",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0004-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 104,
        "start": 104
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It was relatively new. I think the Sullivan Law was 1911. The licensing requirement at issue here was 1913. I think Massachusetts had done something similar in 1906. Hawaii did its as well in 1913."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0004-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 106,
        "start": 106
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But what does that show about the original understanding of the right that's protected by the Second Amendment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0005-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 108,
        "start": 108
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLETCHER: So you're certainly right about the way that Heller looked to decisions to -- on its core holding of does the Second Amendment protect only a militia-focused right or an individual right. But, when Heller turned to the question presented here, which is what sorts of regulations are consistent with the right that it was recognizing, I think it's fairly read to extend the analysis into the 20th Century for the reason that Justice Kagan identified, that it validated as presumptively lawful felon-in-possession requirements, bans on the possession of firearms by the mentally ill that date to much later than the 19th Century."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0005-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 109,
        "start": 109
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What do you do with Heller and its recognition of categories of exclusion? Mentally ill, felons, domestic violence, presumably, although it didn't mention it. Can any of those pass strict scrutiny on their face?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0005-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 112,
        "start": 112
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Fletcher, I -- I think I probably should have asked General Underwood this question, but I forgot, so here you are. And the United States also has law enforcement officers, even though they operate differently from sort of the cop on the beat, but I'm just wondering if there is anything that you can say, any evidence that you can share, are there studies, is there information about how this actually affects how getting rid of -- of this regime in the way that Mr. Clement would want this Court to do, how it affects policing, how it affects the ability of police officers to keep the streets safe and --and how it affects their own safety? Is there information about that? Is there -- are there studies?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1f8a701a0bc-0005-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 115,
        "start": 115
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLETCHER: I appreciate the question, Justice Gorsuch, and I think our view is that courts ought to follow what we understand to be the lesson from Heller, which is that you start with text, history, and tradition, and when those sources provide you an answer one way or the other, either that the law is valid or that it's invalid, you end there and that's the end of the inquiry."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-20-843",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "e1f8a701a0bc54fb034d7205ef127c7ca5c86644e539b4189e6c7e2b57703812",
